  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5751e45b3bc551448917ed569792a2a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Testimony of a surface team member
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  fullText: We were transporting the object as instructed, inside the sealed container,
    when one of the reefs collapsed. We were prepared for such situations, but the
    container was too large to handle comfortably, and got damaged while we moved
    to safety. The second water touched the object, it began moving and emitting
    a red light, followed by a screeching sound. We tried to go back to the surface
    to prevent further damage, but the order was given to completely cover the object
    and rush to Prubei laboratory. I can not figure out what that thing was, but
    I do know one thing... it is not ours.
  currentText: 
  placeFoundText: 
  timeFound: 
  orderToDisplay: 52
